 Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
 | `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }`; the title is saved trimmed | 201, the task, or 400 |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done`; a `title` in the body follows the same rules as on `POST` | 200, the task, 400, or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
-Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
+Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`:
+
+| Status | `error` | When |
+|---|---|---|
+| 400 | `title is required` | `POST`, or `PATCH` with a `title`: the title is missing, not a string, empty or only spaces |
+| 400 | `title must be at most 200 characters` | The trimmed title is longer than 200 characters |
+| 400 | `invalid JSON body` | The request body is not valid JSON |
+| 404 | `task not found` / `not found` | Unknown task or path |
+| 405 | `method not allowed` | |
+| 500 | `internal error` | Unexpected failure; the details are only in the server log |
+
+A valid JSON body that is not an object (`null`, an array, a number) is read as `{}`. On `PATCH`, the title is checked before the task is looked up.
 
 ## Layout
 
 - `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
 - `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
